<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Sound Buddy is local-first. Your audio never leaves your machine. Here's exactly what the app sends — update checks, license refresh, and opt-in diagnostics that are off by default — and what it never sends."
  updated="August 27, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Sound Buddy is built local-first, and privacy is the whole point. This policy explains — in plain
    English — exactly what stays on your Mac and the little that leaves it.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p><strong>No audio data leaves your machine.</strong> Sound Buddy analyzes your recordings
    entirely on your Mac. We never upload, collect, or transmit your audio, and it never touches our
    servers — because we don't run any.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>What stays on your Mac</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your audio.</strong> Recordings, stems, and everything you analyze are processed
      on-device and stored only where you save them.</li>
    <li><strong>Your report cards and analysis.</strong> Grades, metrics, and session data live in
      local files on your machine.</li>
    <li><strong>Your license key.</strong> Stored locally on your device to unlock Pro features.
      It isn't shared or synced anywhere by the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>AI is optional — and yours</h2>
  <p>
    If you turn on the AI analyst, you choose the provider: a local model through Ollama, or your own
    API key for a provider you control. Either way, Sound Buddy does not store your AI prompts or the
    responses, and it never proxies AI requests through us. Whatever you send goes directly to the
    provider you picked, under that provider's own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>What the app sends — and what it never does</h2>
  <p>
    Sound Buddy is local-first, but it is not offline. Here is every outbound connection the app
    makes, what it carries, and what turns it on. If you watch it with Little Snitch, this list
    should match what you see — if it doesn't, tell us and we'll fix the list.
  </p>
  <h3>Always on</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Update check.</strong> On launch, and when you pick Help ▸ Check for Updates…,
      the app asks GitHub whether a newer build exists by reading the public release feed for
      <a href="https://github.com/on-par/sound-buddy-releases" rel="noopener"
        >on-par/sound-buddy-releases</a>. It sends no identifiers of any kind — it's the same
      request your browser would make.</li>
    <li><strong>License refresh.</strong> If you hold a monthly Pro subscription, the app posts
      your already-signed license key — and nothing else — to
      <code>https://soundbuddy.online/api/license/refresh</code> so your key renews without you
      re-pasting it. It runs at launch, when a Pro feature is evaluated, and when you click
      Refresh license. Never on a timer, and never if you don't have a subscription key stored.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Off by default — you turn these on</h3>
  <p>
    All three live under Settings ▸ Privacy (feedback is a dialog you open). Each posts to
    <code>https://soundbuddy.online/api/ingest</code>. Leave them off and the app never contacts
    that endpoint at all.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Share anonymous usage counts</strong> — off by default. When on, the app records
      a fixed, published list of seven event names (things like "app opened" and "analysis
      completed"), stamped to the hour, with a random install identifier that is not derived from
      you, your machine, or your license. No file names, no audio, no free text.</li>
    <li><strong>Send crash reports</strong> — off by default. When on, a crash sends the error
      message, stack trace, app and macOS version, and the recent screen names. Email addresses,
      license keys, and your file paths are stripped before it leaves your Mac, and stripped
      again when it arrives.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback you send us</strong> — never automatic. It sends only what you type,
      plus your app and macOS version, and only when you click Send. If you tick "attach
      diagnostics", a short, redacted tail of the local log goes with it.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>What the app never sends</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>None of these ever carries your audio. Recordings, stems, analysis results, and report
      cards stay on your Mac, always, with every setting on.</li>
    <li>There are no accounts to create and no profiles to track you across the web.</li>
    <li>This website uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless: it sets no cookies,
      stores no device identifiers, and cannot follow you to other sites. It records aggregate
      page views and referrers only — and it runs on the website, not in the app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The waitlist</h2>
  <p>
    If you join the waitlist, we store the email address you enter, the church or ministry name if
    you choose to give one, the date you signed up, and the IP address the signup came from. The IP
    is kept only to rate-limit the form against abuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use that address to confirm your signup, to tell you when early access opens, and to send the
    occasional note about what we're building. That's all. It is never sold, never shared with
    advertisers, and never used to track you anywhere else. Every message has an unsubscribe link,
    and unsubscribing removes you from the list. Email <a href="mailto:support@soundbuddy.online"
      >support@soundbuddy.online</a
    > any time and we'll delete your entry outright.
  </p>
  <p>
    Waitlist email is delivered by <a href="https://resend.com" rel="noopener">Resend</a>, which
    processes your address for that purpose only.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments and your email</h2>
  <p>
    When you buy Sound Buddy Pro, payment is handled by <a href="https://stripe.com" rel="noopener">Stripe</a>,
    a PCI-compliant payment processor. We never see or store your full card details — Stripe does. The
    email address you check out with is used to deliver your license key and to send purchase and
    support messages related to your subscription. It is not sold, and it is not used for unrelated
    marketing. Stripe's handling of your payment data is covered by <a
      href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Stripe's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Support email</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us for support or a refund, we keep that correspondence so we can help you. That's it.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Sound Buddy is a professional audio tool intended for adults and isn't directed at children under 13.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever change what we collect, we'll update this page and the "last updated" date above. Because
    Sound Buddy is local-first by design, our goal is for this policy to stay short.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
